Figure 2 characterizes the Nano-11 nanoparticles, showing them as spherical particles with an irregular surface by TEM (A) and a uniform hydrodynamic diameter of 75-80 nm by DLS (B). The nanoparticles exhibit a positive zeta potential across a wide pH range (C), which facilitates the electrostatic adsorption of negatively charged proteins like ovalbumin (OVA). This selective adsorption is demonstrated in panel D, where Nano-11 efficiently binds OVA but not positively charged lysozyme, confirming its utility for antigen delivery.